  "query_preview": "..\n(Today through next Monday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: \n\nUpper level trough which has provided the much needed rainfall \nover the last few days has finally departed for points east. As \nthe upper trough departs, high pressure will build bringing \nquieter weather back into the region. However, with the quieter \nweather, light winds, and clearing skies will need to watch out \nfor fog and freezing fog in the morning for the valleys given the \nnow very moist ground around the state this ridge will transit the\nstate through Tuesday. Wednesday, the next upper trough is \nexpected to move through Nevada, with central Nevada seeing the \ngreatest potential for precipitation. Wednesday\u2019s system will be \nmoisture starved with only light accumulations possible, as the \nUS-50 corridor could see up to 0.15\u201d of rain with up to 2\u201d of snow\nfor the mountains. Thursday will be another quiet day weather \nwise with models bringing another trough through for Friday \nmorning, although this trough looks to bring only clouds. For next\nweekend Models are not in agreement with the pattern, giving a \nlow confidence forecast past Friday as there is equal potential \nfor an upper ridge, upper troughing, or a mixed flow regime. \nTemperature wise for the holiday weekend and into next week thanks\nto the active pattern will be relatively consistent next week \nthrough Thursday as highs will be near to, to slightly below \nnormal ranging in the mid 40s to upper 50s, with lows in the mid \n20s to upper 30s. After Thursday there is the potential for a slow\nwarming trend with highs rising into the mid 50s to mid 60s next \nweekend. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: \n \nThere is high confidence in upper ridge transiting the great \nbasin Monday and Tuesday which will bring dry conditions and light\nwinds. \n\nThere is medium confidence for an upper level trough passage \nWednesday, with low chances for light valley rainfall and mountain\nsnow for central Nevada. \n     \nThere is low to low confidence of upper pattern evolution after \nFriday as models show varied upper air pattern with either \ntroughing or ridging taking place.",
